<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><h1>Terms and conditions</h1><p>Information for candidates and receiving organisations.</p></div></section><section class="container section prose"><div class="alert alert-warning"><strong>LEGAL REVIEW REQUIRED:</strong> Replace all [LEGAL TEXT REQUIRED] sections with approved, jurisdiction-specific terms before production use.</div><h2>1. Test services</h2><p>GEST operates candidate registration, test booking and results certification for centre-administered assessments. GEST does not deliver examination questions through this website.</p><h2>2. Booking and cancellation</h2><p>Bookings are subject to available seats. Your test centre confirms payment. Candidates may cancel up to the number of days before the session stated in the cancellation policy at the time of cancellation. Contact the centre regarding payments and refunds.</p><p>[LEGAL TEXT REQUIRED: binding refund rules, age of consent, rescheduling, absence, force majeure and accessibility accommodations.]</p><h2>3. Scores and recognition</h2><p>GEST reports four skill scores and an overall score; there is no GEST pass/fail outcome. Recognition or admission is solely at the discretion of the receiving institution.</p><h2>4. Certificates and verification</h2><p>Certificates have an issue and expiry date and may be revoked or reissued. Online verification is the authoritative validity check.</p><h2>5. Candidate conduct</h2><p>Candidates must present authentic identification, provide truthful information and follow their test centre's assessment rules.</p><p>[LEGAL TEXT REQUIRED: malpractice procedures, appeals, score reviews, liability, dispute resolution and governing law.]</p></section>
